 "2026-07-30 12:44:03.453000", "updatedAt": "2026-07-30 12:44:14.834000", "finalisedAt": null, "appointmentId": "cms7huwye006ttb3qy5rcybc6", "voiceTranscript": null}, "prescriptions": [{"id": "cms8ob3d0008ttb3qpwwj0gdq", "items": [{"dose": "1 tablet", "drug": "Amoxicin", "form": "tablet", "duration": "4", "strength": "500mg", "frequency": "BD", "instructions": "ful course"}], "pdfUrl": null, "doctorId": "cmrbv1iyw000113x20yuzqweg", "sharedAt": null, "refillable": true, "refillsRemaining": 1, "interactionAcknowledged": false}], "clinical_output": {"id": "cms7i9hsw008ftb3qfhwkxuuk", "icdCodes": [{"code": "8E11.0", "description": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications"}, {"code": "MD21", "description": "Dizziness"}, {"code": "MB23.2", "description": "Unintentional weight loss"}, {"code": "ML26", "description": "Nonadherence to medical treatment"}], "soapNote": {"plan": "1. Increase Metformin to prescribed dose of 500mg twice daily immediately to improve glycemic control. 2. Educate on importance of medication adherence and potential consequences of uncontrolled diabetes. 3. Monitor blood glucose levels closely (e.g., daily fasting and post-prandial) and track weight. 4. Consider A1c and comprehensive metabolic panel. 5. Discuss dietary and lifestyle modifications for diabetes management. 6. Follow-up in 1-2 weeks to assess medication adherence, symptom improvement, and review lab results. 7. If symptoms persist or worsen despite optimal Metformin dose, consider further investigation for other causes of weight loss/dizziness or escalation of diabetes therapy.", "objective": "Current medication: Metformin 500mg once daily (prescribed twice daily). Known allergies: a. Past medical history includes diabetes (3 months ago), resolved cough, fever, low back pain, and fatigue. No family history of diabetes. Occupation: Farmer.", "assessment": "Uncontrolled Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus likely due to suboptimal medication adherence (Metformin 500mg once daily instead of twice daily), presenting with significant unintentional weight loss and dizziness. The weight loss and dizziness are concerning for hyperglycemia and potential metabolic decompensation.", "subjective": "Mr. Asadiya presents with uncontrolled diabetes symptoms, including dizziness and significant unintentional weight loss (5-6 kg in the past month). He was diagnosed with diabetes 3 months ago following dizziness. He reports taking Metformin 500mg once daily, despite a twice-daily prescription, and has not noticed symptom improvement. Dizziness impacts his ability to perform physically demanding farming duties."}, "snomedCodes": ["Type 2 diabetes mellitus (disorder)", "Dizziness (finding)", "Weight loss (finding)", "Physical demanding activity (qualifier value)", "Metformin (substance)", "Medication adherence problem (finding)"], "recommendations": []}}	{"host": "34.14.174.141:3003", "accept": "*/*", "user-agent": "curl/8.21.0", "content-type": "application/json", "content-length": "25371"}	f	\N	(sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql.asyncpg.Error) <class 'asyncpg.exceptions.DataError'>: invalid input for query argument $1: 'cms7i9919008btb3qjlz2hkid' (invalid UUID 'cms7i9919008btb3qjlz2hkid': length must be between 32..36 characters, got 25)\n[SQL: SELECT id FROM consultations WHERE external_id = $1]\n[parameters: ('cms7i9919008btb3qjlz2hkid',)]\n(Background on this error at: https://sqlalche.me/e/20/dbapi)	\N	2026-08-06 11:44:44.332085+00	2026-08-06 11:44:44.346197+00	\N
