cmrc194jk0057t9jwyyvulcbd", "updatedAt": "2026-07-30 12:32:54.614000", "reasonForVisit": "Onboarding: diabetes", "durationMinutes": 15}, "consultation": {"id": "cms7i9919008btb3qjlz2hkid", "status": "REVIEWED", "doctorId": "cmrbv1iyw000113x20yuzqweg", "noteText": "CHIEF COMPLAINT\\nUncontrolled diabetes symptoms including dizziness and significant unintentional weight loss.\\nOnset: 3 months ago (for diabetes diagnosis) and 1 month ago (for weight loss). · Severity: Impacts ability to perform hard work in farming. · Character: Dizziness described, significant weight loss (5-6 kg in 1 month).\\n\\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\\nMr. Asadiya was diagnosed with diabetes 3 months ago after experiencing dizziness. Since his diagnosis, he has also experienced significant unintentional weight loss, losing 5-6 kg over the past month. He reports taking Metformin 500mg once daily, despite a twice-daily prescription, and has not noticed any change in symptoms since adjusting his medication schedule. The dizziness currently impacts his ability to perform physically demanding farming duties.\\nTimeline: Diabetes diagnosed 3 months ago due to dizziness., Unintentional weight loss of 5-6 kg over 1 month.\\nAggravating: Physically demanding work (farming) makes symptoms worse\\nAlleviating: Not discussed\\nAssociated symptoms: Dizziness, Unintentional weight loss (5-6 kg in 1 month)\\n\\nMEDICATIONS & TREATMENTS\\nCurrent: Metformin 500mg once daily (prescribed twice daily)\\nTried: Metformin - partial adherence, no change in symptoms\\nAllergies: Not discussed\\n\\nRELEVANT HISTORY\\nPast medical: Diabetes (diagnosed 3 months ago), Cough (resolved), Fever (resolved), Low back pain (resolved), Fatigue (resolved)\\nFamily: No family history of diabetes\\nSocial: Farmer (occupation)\\n\\nFUNCTIONAL IMPACT\\nDaily: Dizziness and other symptoms make physically demanding farming duties difficult.\\nWork: Impacts ability to perform hard work in farming.\\nSleep: Not discussed", "createdAt": "2026-07-30 12:44:03.453000", "updatedAt": "2026-07-30 12:44:14.834000", "finalisedAt": null, "appointmentId": "cms7huwye006ttb3qy5rcybc6", "voiceTranscript": null}, "prescriptions": [{"id": "cms8ob3d0008ttb3qpwwj0gdq", "items": [{"dose": "1 tablet", "drug": "Amoxicin", "form": "tablet", "duration": "4", "strength": "500mg", "frequency": "BD", "instructions": "ful course"}], "pdfUrl": null, "doctorId": "cmrbv1iyw000113x20yuzqweg", "sharedAt": null, "refillable": true, "refillsRemaining": 1, "interactionAcknowledged": false}], "clinical_output": {"id": "cms7i9hsw008ftb3qfhwkxuuk", "icdCodes": [{"code": "8E11.0", "description": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications"}, {"code": "MD21", "description": "Dizziness"}, {"code": "MB23.2", "description": "Unintentional weight loss"}, {"code": "ML26", "description": "Nonadherence to medical treatment"}], "soapNote": {"plan": "1. Increase Metformin to prescribed dose of 500mg twice daily immediately to improve glycemic control. 2. Educate on importance of medication adherence and potential consequences of uncontrolled diabetes. 3. Monitor blood glucose levels closely (e.g., daily fasting and post-prandial) and track weight. 4. Consider A1c and comprehensive metabolic panel. 5. Discuss dietary and lifestyle modifications for diabetes management. 6. Follow-up in 1-2 weeks to assess medication adherence, symptom improvement, and review lab results. 7. If symptoms persist or worsen despite optimal Metformin dose, consider further investigation for other causes of weight loss/dizziness or escalation of diabetes therapy.", "objective": "Current medication: Metformin 500mg once daily (prescribed twice daily). Known allergies: a. Past medical history includes diabetes (3 months ago), resolved cough, fever, low back pain, and fatigue. No family history of diabetes. Occupation: Farmer.", "assessment": "Uncontrolled Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus likely due to suboptimal medication adherence (Metformin 500mg once daily instead of twice daily), presenting with significant unintentional weight loss and dizziness. The weight loss and dizziness are concerning for hyperglycemia and potential metabolic decompensation.", "subjective": "Mr. Asadiya presents with uncontrolled diabetes symptoms, including dizziness and significant unintentional weight loss (5-6 kg in the past month). He was diagnosed with diabetes 3 months ago following dizziness. He reports taking Metformin 500mg once daily, despite a twice-daily prescription, and has not noticed symptom improvement. Dizziness impacts his ability to perform physically demanding farming duties."}, "snomedCodes": ["Type 2 diabetes mellitus (disorder)", "Dizziness (finding)", "Weight loss (finding)", "Physical demanding activity (qualifier value)", "Metformin (substance)", "Medication adherence problem (finding)"], "recommendations": []}}	{"host": "34.14.174.141", "accept": "*/*", "x-real-ip": "111.125.253.79", "connection": "close", "user-agent": "curl/8.18.0", "content-type": "application/json", "content-length": "25371", "x-forwarded-for": "111.125.253.79", "x-forwarded-proto": "http"}	t	2026-08-06 13:33:47.473255+00	\N	097cae13-a418-41a8-a104-ab1588b441db	2026-08-06 13:33:47.426351+00	2026-08-06 13:33:47.473255+00	7865d9587b958da964a58163194b79e6aa76249ab6f6f6fe0444f8d6095e51ce
